%S A399981 1,4,24,194,1960,23770,336322,5438496,98936250,1999814916,44464855512,
%T A399981 1078530770196,28340682384300,801997011421320
%N A399981 Total number of standard Young tableaux over all basic skew shapes with n cells. (Row sums of A399982.)
%C A399981 A225114 counts each basic skew shape once, whereas the present sequence weights each shape D by its number f^D of standard Young tableaux.
%D A399981 R. P. Stanley, Enumerative Combinatorics, Vol. 2, Cambridge University Press, 1999; see Corollary 7.16.3.
%F A399981 a(n) <= n * A400280(n) where equality holds in the case where n is prime. - _Peter Luschny_, Sep 23 2026
%e A399981 For n = 2 there are three basic skew shapes: a horizontal domino, a vertical domino, and the two cell diagonal skew shape. The horizontal and vertical dominoes each have one standard Young tableau, while the diagonal shape has two. Hence a(2) = 1 + 1 + 2 = 4.
%Y A399981 Cf. A225114, A399982, A400280.
%K A399981 nonn,more,new
%O A399981 1,2
%A A399981 _Gabriel Michael Chavez_, Sep 17 2026
